  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Catalysing responsible use of artificial intelligence in humanitarian action</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project&#x2014;led by IOM&#x2019;s Global Data Institute (GDI) in partnership with UNHCR, UN OCHA, the Danish Refugee Council (DRC), the Norwegian Refugee Council (NRC), and Luxembourg research partners including the Luxembourg Institute of Science and Technology (LIST) and the University of Luxembourg Institute for Digital Ethics (ULIDE)&#x2014;will accelerate IOM&#x2019;s contributions to critical system-wide assets, thereby catalyzing responsible use of AI across the humanitarian system. It will reinforce IOM&#x2019;s contributions to priority collaborative workstreams being delivered this year through the UN80 Data Quint, through which OCHA, IOM, UNHCR, UNICEF, and WFP are jointly delivering measurable progress in the production and sharing of core data, the joint delivery of advanced analysis, and enhancements in data capacity for operations. IOM and its partners will achieve this through the research, joint development, and convening for collective ownership and validation of a system-wide framework for responsible AI in humanitarian action.</narrative>
  </description>
